{"title":"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Similar_to_Solution_2)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Similar to Solution 2)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Calculus)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Calculus)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> be the smallest <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Integer\" title=\"Integer\">integer</a> whose <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Cube_root\" title=\"Cube root\">cube root</a> is of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/c/f0ca0e65f9bfcde9a55af830c90726460cf46581.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n+r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive_integer\" title=\"Positive integer\">positive integer</a> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is a <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Positive\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Positive\">positive</a> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Real_number\" title=\"Real number\">real number</a> less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/3/ba30132a6117c1401acb42bc3fa665a45d66ae56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In order to keep <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> as small as possible, we need to make <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> as small as possible.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/7/2d7395329be8388eed744234b1ab2ec8fd5c33b1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = (n + r)^3 = n^3 + 3n^2r + 3nr^2 + r^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"303\" height=\"21\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/7/b27104c0fe51032b2f6f065c6e83584c747b5ef3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r &lt; \\frac{1}{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"75\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/5/db5df3389e6e2775fff4f7a4454cecedac7529e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m - n^3 = r(3n^2 + 3nr + r^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"222\" height=\"21\" /> is an integer, we must have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/b/4cba53e580e930d579cca358941e1185647b9c5f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n^2 + 3nr + r^2 \\geq \\frac{1}{r} &gt; 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"217\" height=\"38\" />.  This means that the smallest possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> should be less than 1000. In particular, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/c/73cba7eab146527897ffc47d6d3d9fc69f89d142.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3nr + r^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"69\" height=\"18\" /> should be less than 1, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/b/14be6328a096cd8e70351c757515546de5fe1de1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n^2 &gt; 999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"81\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/a/72a4704716581f5b72137c345e0317ed760a8de6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n &gt; \\sqrt{333}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"79\" height=\"21\" />.  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/d/23d109d7e9e9d2b010f045e5408c5c370c157caf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$18^2 = 324 &lt; 333 &lt; 361 = 19^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"232\" height=\"18\" />, so we must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/4/674ad89dde9bc458e09f5003b3d1e6030e293fd7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"55\" height=\"16\" />.  Since we want to minimize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, we take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/e/8aeed81ffe5071b2d5d291bca220b3480da708cb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"55\" height=\"14\" />.  Then for any positive value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/a/eda6efc8eb34b4791ed44a2ee8675fc00cf0142c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n^2 + 3nr + r^2 &gt; 3\\cdot 19^2 &gt; 1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"251\" height=\"18\" />, so it is possible for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> to be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d66aef8e879a5ef4d466264feaecf4737683e0de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"42\" height=\"38\" />.  However, we still have to make sure a sufficiently small <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> exists.  \n</p><p>In light of the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/5/db5df3389e6e2775fff4f7a4454cecedac7529e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m - n^3 = r(3n^2 + 3nr + r^2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"222\" height=\"21\" />, we need to choose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/f/92fff9671355f6cb140d3b21314375f1df1b6a74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m - n^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> as small as possible to ensure a small enough <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.  The smallest possible value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/f/92fff9671355f6cb140d3b21314375f1df1b6a74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m - n^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> is 1, when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/d/62d954bf867eae5de72c43c59d5668a16db7f8db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = 19^3 + 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"99\" height=\"18\" />.  Then for this value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/3/9435df37c80e8b9de32a8d7700c1fa03269f8f84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{1}{3n^2 + 3nr + r^2} &lt; \\frac{1}{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"220\" height=\"40\" />, and we're set.  The answer is  <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/6/b56e3ea833b92b1d8057d6a08efa889826dacd96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{019}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>To minimize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />, we should minimize <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />. We have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/d/15de84eb5c7a3ab9685ddaca8cb8d069a3a595e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n + \\frac{1}{1000})^3 = n^3 + \\frac{3}{10^3} n^2 + \\frac{3}{10^6} n + \\frac{1}{10^9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"324\" height=\"38\" />. For a given value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3373fd2eefee1a04b2452b7f9a7bb184aa5920ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n + \\frac{1}{1000})^3 - n^3 &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"171\" height=\"38\" />, there exists an integer between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/7/b579d00c2af1ce8fd026bd31ec8ba4438a9dc739.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n + \\frac{1}{1000})^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"97\" height=\"38\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/a/4ba37f50c674bcbae995ed1d9dfd4beb5e53c765.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" />, and the cube root of this integer would be between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/a/f8a932f5734bcb1d295dadbed439f6cb90cd434a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n + \\frac{1}{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"75\" height=\"38\" /> as desired. We seek the smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3373fd2eefee1a04b2452b7f9a7bb184aa5920ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n + \\frac{1}{1000})^3 - n^3 &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"171\" height=\"38\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/0/3904c013c56db7529f57feb485194a527dbaf1f1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(n + \\frac{1}{1000})^3 - n^3 &gt; 1\\]\" width=\"166\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/3/c432a86ac0878eaba35a4b5b157f0c9c185ab84a.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{3}{10^3} n^2 + \\frac{3}{10^6} n + \\frac{1}{10^9} &gt; 1\\]\" width=\"193\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/e/0ee738a2d6c25168c205f7a8f10d660a099dd900.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[3n^2 + \\frac{3}{10^3} n + \\frac{1}{10^6} &gt; 10^3\\]\" width=\"190\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Trying values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />, we see that the smallest value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> that works is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/6/b56e3ea833b92b1d8057d6a08efa889826dacd96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{019}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>Why is it <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3373fd2eefee1a04b2452b7f9a7bb184aa5920ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n + \\frac{1}{1000})^3 - n^3 &gt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"171\" height=\"38\" /> and not greater than or equal to? - awesomediabrine\n</p><p>Because if its equal to, then there is no integer in between the two values. - resources\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Similar_to_Solution_2.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Similar_to_Solution_2)\">Solution 3 (Similar to Solution 2)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Similar to Solution 2)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/3/ba30132a6117c1401acb42bc3fa665a45d66ae56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1/1000$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" />, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/9/549f6587b55cb788432530b0816b2f7e21ad7cb4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sqrt[3]{m} &lt; n + \\frac{1}{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"131\" height=\"38\" />. Notice that since we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> minimized, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> should also be minimized. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/a/4ba37f50c674bcbae995ed1d9dfd4beb5e53c765.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"17\" /> should be as close as possible, but not exceeding <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />. This means <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> should be set to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/7/d471274214d66e1cbb4070976246802aa421f063.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n^3+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"18\" />. Substituting and simplifying, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/8/8a82a0445f234914aa9316660b30fe2a27864e79.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt[3]{n^3+1} &lt; n + \\frac{1}{1000}\\]\" width=\"159\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/e/dfe53e3267c622099aeb923653190a80fabb9259.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n^3+1 &lt; n^3+\\frac{3}{1000}n^2+\\frac{3}{1000^2}n+\\frac{1}{1000^3}\\]\" width=\"321\" height=\"37\" />\nThe last two terms in the right side can be ignored in the calculation because they are too small. This results in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/5/14572b1eddfe2212e1d278f64d26634e520f655d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1 &lt; \\frac{3}{1000}n^2 \\Rightarrow n^2 &gt; \\frac{1000}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"205\" height=\"38\" />. The minimum positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> that satisfies this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/6/b56e3ea833b92b1d8057d6a08efa889826dacd96.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{019}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"40\" height=\"25\" />. ~ Hb10\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Calculus.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Calculus)\">Solution 4 (Calculus)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Calculus)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the cube root is increasing for positive reals while its derivative is decreasing, so linear approximation gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/1/b8199dd7c0b883252e3a361f6fb25accd1379833.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt[3]{n^3+1} - n &lt; \\left.\\frac{d\\sqrt[3]{x}}{dx}\\right|_{x=n^3} = \\frac{1}{3n^2}\\]\" width=\"255\" height=\"44\" />\nand\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ecea7387a041920fb6e5d4530471d4733ecd7cf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\sqrt[3]{n^3+1} - n &gt; \\left.\\frac{d\\sqrt[3]{x}}{dx}\\right|_{x=n^3+1} = \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{(n^3+1)^2}}\\]\" width=\"344\" height=\"46\" />\nFrom this, it is clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/b/00bc87e3506b6863486b2f1ac14b901124f4ff1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\boxed{019}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"76\" height=\"25\" /> is the smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for which LHS will be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/6/d66aef8e879a5ef4d466264feaecf4737683e0de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{1000}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"42\" height=\"38\" />. ~ Hyprox1413\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME\" title=\"1987 AIME\">1987 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1987 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1987\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1987_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1987 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017180149\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time 